---@class cloudflare.intel.GetDomainBulkRequest
---@field account_id string Identifier.
---@field domain? cloudflare.intel.DomainsBulksGetRequestDomainList Accepts multiple values like `?domain=cloudflare.com&domain=example.com`.
---@field include_ranking? boolean Whether to include domain ranking data in the response. Defaults to `false` — ranking lookups are expensive at bulk scale and most callers do not need them. Set to `true` to opt in. This parameter replaces the deprecated `skip_ranking` (see below).
---@field skip_dns? boolean Skip the DNS resolution-history lookup for faster responses. Defaults to `false`. Set to `true` if you only need categorization data; no DNS resolution history is returned for any domain. Matches the `skip_dns` parameter on `/intel/domain`.
---@field skip_ranking? boolean **Deprecated.** Previously controlled whether the ranking lookup was skipped (defaulted to `false`, meaning ranking ran). The endpoint's default behavior is being flipped — ranking is now opt-in via `include_ranking=true` — and this parameter will be silently ignored. Remove it from your callers and use `include_ranking` instead.

